%S A398341 0,0,0,2,0,3,0,4,6,5,0,8,0,7,10,12,0,12,0,15,14,11,0,18,20,13,18,21,0,
%T A398341 24,0,24,22,17,28,30,0,19,26,32,0,35,0,33,36,23,0,40,42,40,34,39,0,45,
%U A398341 44,48,38,29,0,50,0,31,54,56,52,55,0,51,46,60,0,63,0,37,60,57,66,65,0,70
%N A398341 a(n) is the number of die sizes < n that can produce n as the product of two identical dice.
%C A398341 Here two identical m-sided dice are each labeled 1, ..., m.
%C A398341 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of zero-based (m+1) X (m+1) multiplication tables in which n occurs and the quotient of n upon division by (m+1) is nonzero.
%C A398341 The zero terms occur exactly at n = 1 and for prime n.
%C A398341 Every prime p occurs exactly once as a value, namely a(2*p) = p.
%C A398341 For n > 1, a(n)/(n-1) is the probability that n occurs in a uniformly chosen positive-indexed multiplication table of size m < n.
%H A398341 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398341/b398341.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398341 Frédéric D. W. Heidenthal-König, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18960358">Euclidean Decomposition of the Multiplication Table</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398341 Frédéric D. W. Heidenthal-König, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19390886">On the Motion of Numbers</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A398341 a(n) = n - A033677(n).
%F A398341 gcd(n, a(n)) = A033677(n) = n - a(n).
%F A398341 a(n) + A395409(n) = n - A135034(n) = n - ceiling(sqrt(n)).
%F A398341 a(n) = 0 iff n = 1 or n is prime.
%F A398341 If p is prime, a(2*p) = p. Conversely, if a(n) is prime, then n = 2*a(n).
%e A398341 a(36) = 30, since 36 can occur as the product of rolls of two m-sided dice for m = 6, 7, ..., 35 before 36 itself becomes a face.
%e A398341 a(p) = 0: A prime p cannot occur as a product of two rolls on dice with fewer than p faces.
%t A398341 A398341[n_] := n - #[[Quotient[Length[#], 2] + 1]] & [Divisors[n]];
%t A398341 Array[A398341, 100] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 08 2026 *)
%o A398341 (Python)
%o A398341 from math import isqrt
%o A398341 def a(n):
%o A398341     d = isqrt(n)
%o A398341     while n % d:
%o A398341         d -= 1
%o A398341     return n - n//d
%o A398341 print([a(n) for n in range(1, 81)])
%Y A398341 Cf. A033677, A395409, A135034.
%K A398341 nonn,easy,new
%O A398341 1,4
%A A398341 _Frédéric D. W. Heidenthal-König_, Sep 01 2026
